  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore `.map()`\r\n\r\nScroll through the code in the `script.js` file and make some observations. \r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n- Look at the `travelDeals` array.\r\n- Find the `.map()` code.\r\n- Look at the cards on the page.\r\n\r\n### Think:\r\n\r\n::: details [ How many cards are created?]\r\nThree cards. One card is created for each object in the `travelDeals` array.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [What is changing in each card?]\r\nThe deal information changes. Each card gets a different image, destination, duration, and price from the current object.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [What seems to be repeating?]\r\nThe same `createCard()` function runs for every travel deal. The code repeats the same steps, but uses different data each time.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
